# Meta: rules for rules

- When the user asks to create or change a rule, **or** a correction must stick for later sessions → always add or edit a `.mdc` under `.cursor/rules/`.
- **Numbering** (kebab-case): `001–099` Core/Security/PR gates, `100–199` Integrations/APIs, `200–299` Architecture, `300–399` UI, `800–899` Workflows/Testing.
- **`description`:** ATO (Action, Trigger, Outcome), **≤120 characters**, **English** (see `010-english-content.mdc`).
- **`globs`:** No spaces after commas, no quotes — e.g. `globs: *.ts,src/**/*.tsx`.
- **Length:** Rules **≤200 lines**. Do not duplicate code — point at `@PATH` (e.g. `@src/services/apiKeyService.ts`).
- **Merge policy:** Dual gate lives in `docs/pr-merge-gate.md` (human) and `.cursor/rules/011-coderabbit-pr-gate.mdc` step 7 (authoritative predicate). `013` restates; **do not invent a second predicate**.
- **Examples:** `<example>` and `<example type="invalid">` for allowed vs forbidden patterns.
- **Rule lint:** Scope matches the body; recursive globs where needed; no empty or ambiguous `globs`.

## Catalog (do not fork these)

| Rule | Role |
| ---- | ---- |
| `001` | Secrets, vault, sanitization |
| `010` | English-only repo content |
| `011` | Authoritative merge-quiescence predicate |
| `012` | Dependabot processing |
| `013` | Correction-loop procedure (restates `011`) |
| `100` | Providers + PubMed/arXiv (ADR 0008 façade) |
| `101` | Dexie schema / migrations |
| `102` | External-call resilience |
| `200` | File size, KISS/DRY, Redux |
| `300` | UI, a11y, i18n, Tailwind v4 |
| `800` | Deterministic tests; CI-first full suites |
| `850` | PRD / meeting notes / MCP |

<example>

```yaml
---
description: Block secrets in src; editing services or settings; safe commits and reviews
globs: src/**/*.ts,src/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---
```

</example>

<example type="invalid">

```yaml
globs: "*.tsx", src/**/*.ts
```

Spaces after commas and quoted glob lists are forbidden.

